Held, not built: F2, F3 and F12 (they wait on HP; HPSMPOC-476, -486, -493), the reviewer's two titles, any added question or dropped question, any change to readiness, and the HTML-phase and next-phase items. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** (Step 1; a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). No message to any human. **Jira: 0 reads, 0 writes.** No PR (Tuesday opens and lands it through CodeQL: never bypass, never dismiss an alert). No `az`, no ssh, no deploy, and no HTTP to any hosted, demo, UAT or production host; every measurement is on the local build and the two local containers. Never delete (`rm`, `branch -d`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`, `sed -i`): MOVE to `.tools/b1597/_quarantine/`; no amend, rebase or force-push. **No new user-readable word but W1-W5.** **This phase builds no integration with HP tools (Security Manager API, Fleet Threat Assessment, firmware tools, SIEM); next-phase items are stored and architected only, and none of this is ever shown to HP as done.** **Git identity is never overridden:** the repo's own configured identity only; never `git -c user.name/user.email`, never `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*`. No `cd` (a hook refuses it): absolute single-quoted paths (`!CODING` contains `!`), `git -C ... --no-optional-locks` for reads, `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count, python `-I -B`. Every count, `file:line` and clock in STATUS is printed by a program. A closed list is stated by its PROPERTY first and then "at least these"; any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP. `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a failure is fixed at the root and re-verified, never skipped (the one named flaky test is recorded, run at BASE and head, and is not yours to fix).

## CONTEXT BAND AND HANDOVER
This kit is long. At about 70% context start no new step. At about 75% stop at a safe boundary (files whole, both containers stopped by name, every `next start`, stub and Playwright process you started stopped by pid, 10120-10129 free, the lock released) and write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-15_B1597_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps: base sha, branch head if pushed, the four hashes, the census paths, the Q-answers applied), last line `HANDOVER B1597: next step <n> | done steps <list>`, and end STATUS with the same line.

## HARD STOP (slot)
At the HARD STOP clock of the Stamp: start nothing new, push nothing unproven; a committed but unpushed head is `CODED-UNPROVEN b1597/hpsmpoc-lane-q-question-set <sha40>` in STATUS with the steps that ran; write the HANDOVER and end on its line.

## STATUS and the last line
Sections: STATUS-NOW at the top; BLUF; slots as read; PRIOR WORK; BASE (Step 2 rcs and counts, the census); BUILT (files, the four hashes, the deep-diff paths, the ask order); the dynamic census; TESTS (rewritten rows, new rows red-then-green); CI results at BASE and head (each predicate, counts, per shard and part, flaky rows, the known flaky test's counts); the CodeQL pre-scan rows; NOT RUN (the live-API set, C# CodeQL if it cannot extract, with the reason); FOR TUESDAY (the deploy notes; any imprecision of this kit with its line); resources created and removed; the outside-the-fences disclosure. **LAST line, exactly one of:** `READY B1597: <head sha40>` (equal to `git ls-remote` of the branch), `HANDOVER B1597: next step <n> | done steps <list>`, `STOPPED: <reason>` or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`. While running the last line is `PROGRESS B1597: <step>`.

